Subject: PPLs without power

   The current PPLs I see being proposed are nothing more than "playing
house" They have no real power and there is little consequence to NOT
joining one (being an outlaw has no consequence)


   Here is my proposal to remedy this situation:

1) PPL owners will be able to remove the posting ability of their clients
2) PPL owners will have a "super exclude" which overrides any of their
client's settings. (e.g. they can ban Pandit Singh from being seen
by _any_ of their clients. Sorta like kicking him off the list. also,
one PPL can exclude another PPL meaning any posters from a rogue PPL
will not be seen by yours)
3) if you are an outlaw (not a member of a PPL), then you will be
subject to a "1 warning rule"  Simply put, if you are not a member of
a PPL (no protection), then any PPL on the list can "hunt you down" and
"shoot you" That is, any PPL owner can remove your posting
ability but they can not reinstate it (because you're dead)

   If you have been shot, your only recourse is to join a PPL and be
resurrected (the PPL owner can turn on your posting ability if you're
a client)


  Inter-PPL threats could take the form of releasing "criminals"
(previously banned posters) on the other PPL.

4) when the list goes to a "for pay" system, part of the subscription
free will go into your list account as list currency which is tradable
like thornes. Only if your list credits go to zero will you be required
to renew your subscription (posting/receiving mail deducts credits
as does list services like AGREPing the database and resending)

5) to prevent outlaws from simply forming PPLs themselves to prevent
being shot, a minimal membership requirement will need to be met before
the anti-shooting protection kicks in.


  If these proposals were enacted, we could eliminate Harry's fiat
regulation and have PPL's spontaneously self regulate because of market
conditions and internalized costs. PPL's would have real "guns" and
powr instead of relying on members to shut their mouths or begging
Harry to remove them from the list.

-Ray
p.s. this is only my proposal and has nothin to do to with Harry or official
ExI plans



